[1] SOLVER
------------------------------------------------------------------
system/controlDict (excerpt):

    application     buoyantSimpleFoam;

Formulation:
  - buoyantSimpleFoam is a steady, incompressible-approx solver
    that treats buoyancy via the Boussinesq approximation
    (rho held at rho_0; density variation appears only in the
    momentum body-force term as rho_0 * beta * (T - T_ref) * g).
  - Single fluid region. Single-phase air. No species transport.
  - Pressure-velocity coupling by SIMPLE with under-relaxation.

Rationale (per CPL_case_validation_note.pdf):
    Interior building airflow at design supply velocities is
    weakly buoyant, essentially incompressible, and non-reacting.
    Boussinesq is inside its envelope for the isothermal-to-within
    6 degC condition documented in the validation note.


[2] TURBULENCE
------------------------------------------------------------------
constant/turbulenceProperties:

    simulationType  RAS;

constant/RASProperties:

    RASModel        kEpsilon;
    turbulence      on;
    printCoeffs     on;

Wall treatment:
    Standard wall functions on all no-slip walls:
        k        -> kqRWallFunction
        epsilon  -> epsilonWallFunction
        nut      -> nutkWallFunction

Note:
    k-epsilon with standard wall functions is the firm default for
    HVAC interior air. Validated for this project's geometry and
    supply-air range per the case validation note.


[3] INLET BOUNDARY CONDITION (supply diffuser face)
------------------------------------------------------------------
0/U (excerpt):

    inlet
    {
        type            fixedValue;
        value           uniform (0.4 0 0);   // 0.4 m/s along +x
    }

Nominal supply-air velocity: 0.4 m/s at the diffuser boundary.
Inside the validated envelope of 0.2-0.8 m/s.

0/T (excerpt):

    inlet
    {
        type            fixedValue;
        value           uniform 293.15;      // 20 degC supply
    }


[4] SOURCE TERMS (fvModels / fvOptions)
------------------------------------------------------------------
system/fvModels:

    // (empty -- no active model entries)

system/fvOptions:

    // (empty -- no active source-term entries)

No reacting-flow chemistry entries. No heat-release source terms.
No species source terms. No mass sources. The momentum, energy
and turbulence equations carry only their native buoyant / viscous
/ turbulence-production contributions -- nothing else is added.

No chemistryProperties dictionary is present in constant/.


[5] OPTICAL / RADIATIVE TRANSPORT
------------------------------------------------------------------
constant/ contents (files present):

    transportProperties
    turbulenceProperties
    RASProperties
    g

The optical transport dictionary is intentionally NOT present in
this case. Interior building air at design conditions is optically
thin over the room scale and the walls are treated as adiabatic
(see [6]), so optical exchange is not modelled in this envelope.


[6] EXTERNAL WALL BOUNDARY CONDITIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------
0/p_rgh (external walls):

    externalWalls
    {
        type            fixedFluxPressure;
        value           uniform 0;
    }

0/T (external walls):

    externalWalls
    {
        type            zeroGradient;   // adiabatic
    }

0/U (external walls):

    externalWalls
    {
        type            noSlip;
    }

External building envelope walls are adiabatic in this case:
zero-gradient temperature (no through-wall heat flux modelled),
paired with fixedFluxPressure so the momentum boundary sees a
consistent hydrostatic pressure gradient under buoyancy. This
matches the validation-note assumption that on the timescale of
the steady interior-airflow solve, envelope conduction is small
compared to interior mixing.


